			<div class="content" id="post-content-4860086">
									

<p>I'll throw a few comments in before this goes away&#8230;</p>
<p>&#8212; A couple very basic pet peeves:</p>
<p>No SCP should be allowed to wander around the containment site.</p>
<p>When something &quot;appears&quot; to do or be something, the implication is it is/does something completely different and the actual thing should be interesting enough to elaborate on somewhere in the article.</p>
<p>&#8212; The &quot;Dr. Wondertainment&quot; aspect doesn't really suit this object and feels tacked on.</p>
<p>&#8212; This guy is pretty much a living Mood Ring, which is somewhat amusing but you need to take that somewhere interesting. Since it's a pretty straightforward anomalous effect, maybe the way to go is to give him a good backstory. I was hoping to see that in the interview, but it didn't really add anything. There wasn't a hook on this one to make it at all memorable.</p>

