<p><strong>Summoned via PM:</strong></p>
<p>Hi there TPE_gaming. Let’s take a look at your concept.</p>
<p>I do see potential here. You’ve crafted an emotional narrative that explains the origins of the scp quite while. I’m also clear about the themes you wish to convey. Before I offer the greenlight, however, I do feel there are a couple of bumps you need to smooth out:</p>
<blockquote>
<p>The nine sheep are living embodiments of nine identical music boxes that contain the mental essence of a child that suffered from fatal familial insomnia.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>One of my major question marks: why are musical boxes morphing into sheep, and vice-versa. I know you’re trying to go for multiple objects as symbols here, but the more you stretch the reader’s imagination, the harder it is to keep them invested in your world. Why not, for example, just take the musical boxes out of the equation? Have the kid still linked to the sheep in some way (maybe he grew up on a farm, for example) and after his death, his spirit lived on in the animals who were his only companions. Or something like that. I just felt the musical boxes were completely random and unnecessary. But I would also like to hear your thoughts and justification if need be.</p>
<p>If you decide to revise the concept / respond below, do drop me another PM and I’ll try to take another look. All the best for now!</p>

